Usage: realpath [OPTION]... [FILE]...

Print the resolved absolute path for each FILE. If no FILE is given,
print the resolved absolute path of the current directory.

All components of the path must exist (no symlinks are followed).
The last component may be non-existent.

Options:
  -E, --canonicalize           all but the last component must exist
  -m, --canonicalize-missing   no path components need to exist
  -e, --canonicalize-existing   all components must exist
  -L, --logical                 resolve '..' before symlinks (accepted)
  -P, --physical                resolve symlinks before '..' (accepted)
  -q, --quiet                   suppress most error messages
  -s, --strip, --no-symlinks    do not expand symlinks
      --relative-to=DIR         print the resolved path relative to DIR
      --relative-base=DIR       print relative paths below DIR
  -z, --zero                    end output with NUL instead of newline

OPTIONS:
  -e, --canonicalize-existing  all components of the path must exist
  -E, --canonicalize           all components but the last must exist
  -m, --canonicalize-missing   no path components need to exist
  -L, --logical                resolve '..' and '.' before symlinks
  -P, --physical               resolve symlinks before '..' and '.'
  -q, --quiet                  suppress error messages
  -s, --strip                  do not expand symlinks
      --no-symlinks            do not expand symlinks
      --relative-to ARG        print the resolved path relative to DIR
      --relative-base ARG      print relative paths below DIR
  -z, --zero                   end output with NUL byte instead of newline
      --help                   display this help and exit
  -V, --version                output version information and exit

EXIT STATUS:
  0  if OK,
  1  if minor problems,
  2  if serious trouble.

WinuxCmd is a Windows implementation of GNU CoreUtils for Linux-Windows developers and AI coding assistants.
